From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:42:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 065/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: enable the
 USB3/DP QMP PHY
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The board deliberately dropped the QMP combo PHY from usb_1_dwc3's phys
list ("Remove USB3 phy", maximum-speed = "high-speed",
qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk), so USB has only ever run at USB2 speed
here, and the typec connector had no orientation-switch port at all.

That comment on qcom_pmic_typec_port_set_polarity() says polarity is
handled separately by phy-qcom-qmp.c — this board never gave it the
chance to. Enable usb_1_qmpphy (reusing the vdda_usb_ss_dp_core/
vdda_usb_ss_dp_1p2 rails already defined on this board) and wire its
orientation-switch endpoint to the typec connector's second port,
mirroring the working sm7150-google-sunfish recipe. Restores USB3
SuperSpeed and gives the connector a real orientation-switch path.

Verified building cleanly (dtc, no new warnings) for
sm7150-xiaomi-surya-huaxing. Not yet verified on real hardware whether
this also fixes OTG/host-mode CC attach detection for source-role
peripherals (investigated at length: CC_ATTACHED/TYPE_C_MISC_STATUS_REG
and TYPE_C_STATE_MACHINE_STATUS_REG never assert with two different
OTG adapters on this same board's port, both at the mainline TCPM
driver level and reading the raw regmap directly, so that may be an
unrelated hardware-level issue).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi   | 23 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index adbf3c0fb..d42867d3c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -671,6 +671,13 @@ pm6150_role_switch_in: endpoint {
 					remote-endpoint = <&usb_1_dwc3_hs>;
 				};
 			};
+
+			port@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+				pm6150_typec_mux_in: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&usb_1_qmpphy_out>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
@@ -993,17 +1000,12 @@ &ufs_mem_phy {
 };
 
 &usb_1 {
-	qcom,select-utmi-as-pipe-clk;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &usb_1_dwc3 {
 	dr_mode = "otg";
 	usb-role-switch;
-	maximum-speed = "high-speed";
-	/* Remove USB3 phy */
-	phys = <&usb_1_hsphy>;
-	phy-names = "usb2-phy";
 };
 
 &usb_1_dwc3_hs {
@@ -1017,6 +1019,17 @@ &usb_1_hsphy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&usb_1_qmpphy {
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vdda_usb_ss_dp_1p2>;
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vdda_usb_ss_dp_core>;
+	orientation-switch;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&usb_1_qmpphy_out {
+	remote-endpoint = <&pm6150_typec_mux_in>;
+};
+
 &venus {
 	//status = "okay";
 };
